## Step 1: Extract and Filter the API Endpoints
Run this command to search through the aapt string pools you dumped earlier. This will instantly pull out any production servers, staging/sandbox gateways, and third-party tracking APIs embedded in both apps:

cd /home/user/Downloads/waydroid_extracted_apks

echo "=== MYMTN CAMEROON ENDPOINTS ===" > mtn_discovered_apis.txt
grep -E -o "https?://[a-zA-Z0-9./?=&_-]+" com.mtn.mtncmr3_strings.txt | sort -u >> mtn_discovered_apis.txt

echo -e "\n=== MTN MOMO CONSUMER ENDPOINTS ===" >> mtn_discovered_apis.txt
grep -E -o "https?://[a-zA-Z0-9./?=&_-]+" mtnft.momo.consumer_strings.txt | sort -u >> mtn_discovered_apis.txt
# Display the findings on your screen
cat mtn_discovered_apis.txt

Look closely at the output for domain variations like mtn.cm, ericsson, or references to financial microservices.
