## Step 2: Audit Shared Preferences & Local Pin Storage (Waydroid Database)
When you use these apps inside Waydroid, they store local session tokens, user profiles, and sometimes obfuscated device fingerprints in plain XML files. Let's look inside their live container sandbox.
Open a terminal on your host machine and access the Waydroid data partition directly:

cd ~/.local/share/waydroid/data/data/

Now check what files they have created on your system:

* For MyMTN Cameroon:

ls -la com.mtn.mtncmr3/shared_prefs/

* For MTN MoMo:

ls -la mtnft.momo.consumer/shared_prefs/


If you see XML files inside these folders, you can read them with cat filename.xml to see if your phone number, account balance caches, or session hashes are stored insecurely.
